Provenance
----------

Zore View is an independent implementation. Its source code, UI drawing and
strings were written for this project: the tree contains no code, icons,
skins, bitmaps or strings copied from any other image viewer. Behaviour was
compared against publicly observable applications, which copyright does not
protect (ideas, procedures and methods of operation).

Third-party components
----------------------

Zore View links the following components. Full license texts are shipped in
`THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/` in every release package; the source tree keeps them
under `third_party/licenses/`.

| Component | Version | License | Used for | License text |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| FreeImage | 3.18.x | GPLv3 (dual: FIPL / GPLv2+) | Fallback decoding (ICO/CUR, TGA/PCX/PNM/XBM/XPM) | `FreeImage-FIPL-1.0.txt` |
| libjpeg (IJG, bundled with FreeImage) | 9c | IJG license | JPEG path inside FreeImage | `LibJPEG-IJG.txt` |
| LibRaw | 0.21.5 | LGPL-2.1 (used) or CDDL-1.0 (dual) | Camera RAW decoding | `LibRaw-LGPL-2.1.txt`, `LibRaw-CDDL-1.0.txt` |
| zlib | 1.2.11 | zlib license | PSD ZIP inflate | `zlib-1.2.11.txt` |

System components provided by Windows (not redistributed): Windows Imaging
Component (WIC), Direct3D 11, Direct2D, DirectWrite, DXGI and the Windows
Shell APIs. They are used through the operating system and are covered by the
Windows license.

Distribution notes
------------------

* FreeImage is statically linked under its **GPLv3** option (FreeImage is dual
  licensed: FIPL or GPLv2/v3), which is compatible with this program's GPL-3.0.
  Its license text still ships with every binary.
* LibRaw is statically linked under LGPL-2.1 (LibRaw's LGPL-2.1 section 3 allows
  relicensing under GPLv2-or-later, so it is compatible with GPL-3.0).
* zlib and libjpeg require attribution and their license texts only.
* Zore View makes no network requests and has no telemetry. See
  `PRIVACY.md` (shipped with every release package).
